$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=encnatlem3  LOC_AFTER=?

* Lemma for encodeNat: the integer part of the binary logarithm of a positive integer is a nonnegative integer.

s1::2z |- 2 e. ZZ
i2::uzid
s3:s1,i2:ax-mp |- 2 e. ( ZZ>= ` 2 )
s4:s3:a1i |- ( N e. NN -> 2 e. ( ZZ>= ` 2 ) )
s5::nnrp |- ( N e. NN -> N e. RR+ )
i6::relogbzcl
s7:s4,s5,i6:syl2anc |- ( N e. NN -> ( 2 logb N ) e. RR )
s8::nnge1 |- ( N e. NN -> 1 <_ N )
i9::logbge0b
s10:s4,s5,i9:syl2anc |- ( N e. NN -> ( 0 <_ ( 2 logb N ) <-> 1 <_ N ) )
s11:s8,s10:mpbird |- ( N e. NN -> 0 <_ ( 2 logb N ) )
i12::flge0nn0
qed:s7,s11,i12:syl2anc |- ( N e. NN -> ( |_ ` ( 2 logb N ) ) e. NN0 )
$)
